UPDATE companies SET description='CARDONE Industries was founded in 1970 by Michael Cardone Sr. and Michael Cardone Jr. in a North Philadelphia storefront. The company began as a remanufacturer of windshield wiper motors, a venture the automotive industry initially dismissed as impossible.

The company specializes in remanufacturing and supplying aftermarket automotive components. Its product lines include power steering components, brake boosters, rack and pinion assemblies, ABS components, brake calipers, drive and prop shafts, control modules, and throttle bodies. The remanufacturing process involves thorough cleaning and inspection of every component, rebuilding with strengthened wear areas and improved designs to prevent future failures, and rigorous functional testing.

Its customers send in underperforming parts for remanufacturing, and the company also provides new replacement components. The business focuses on automotive electronics and mechanical systems, with technical content and training resources aimed at service professionals.

The company’s founding mission was to fix what fails in the auto industry by building better parts backed by better service. Since its inception, CARDONE has operated on sustainability principles—reduce, reuse, recycle—treating remanufacturing as an environmental responsibility. In 2023, the company received a Content Excellence Award at the Knowledge Exchange Conference.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO9001','ISO14001','IATF16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Automotive component remanufacturing", "Component cleaning and inspection", "Design improvement and wear-area strengthening", "Rigorous functional testing", "Warranty claims processing", "Online account self-service (Bill of Lading Generator, Returns Portal)", "Product catalog and pricing management", "Technical training and content publishing"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Automotive electronics", "Auto repair", "Parts distribution"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Remanufacturing process that strengthens wear areas and improves original designs", "Rigorous functional testing of every remanufactured component", "Sustainability commitment: Reduce, Reuse, Recycle since 1970", "Over 50 years of experience in automotive aftermarket parts", "2023 Knowledge Exchange Conference Content Excellence Award"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1970 by Michael Cardone Sr. and Jr. in North Philadelphia -> /", "Remanufacturing process: clean, inspect, rebuild, strengthen wear areas, improve design, test -> /", "Product lines: power steering components, brake boosters, rack and pinion, ABS components, brake calipers, drive/prop shafts, control modules, throttle bodies -> /", "Certifications: ISO9001, ISO14001, IATF16949 -> db", "Headquarters: Philadelphia, Pennsylvania -> db", "Sustainability: Reduce, Reuse, Recycle since day one -> /", "Award: 2023 Knowledge Exchange Conference Content Excellence Award -> /", "Customers: auto shops send parts for rema