UPDATE companies SET description='CED Burlington operates from Williston, Vermont, as part of a national electrical distribution network that traces its roots to 1957 when the first Consolidated Electrical Distributors (CED) location opened in California. The company has since grown to nearly 800 branches across the United States, each empowered to make local stocking and service decisions while leveraging the broader organization’s purchasing power.

The Williston branch stocks and supplies a wide range of electrical equipment including gear packages, service entrance materials, load centers, disconnects, meter mains, and circuit breakers with GFCI, AFCI, and dual-function variants. Beyond product distribution, the location provides value-added services: a licensed lighting designer develops multi-layer residential lighting plans; estimators perform takeoffs from electrical drawings; project managers offer custom reporting with shipping dates and delivery tracking; and the facility provides customer storage with staged delivery to job sites. Emergency same-day delivery and after-hours weekend availability are also offered.

The branch primarily serves residential and commercial electrical contractors, positioning itself as the “Residential Contractors’ Supplier of Choice.” Its gear package capabilities also support larger commercial and industrial projects requiring service entrance equipment and switchgear. Contractors rely on the branch for both standard stock items and hard-to-find components sourced through the national CED network.

CED’s founding motto—“Service. Integrity. Reliability.”—drives its operational philosophy. Local managers have authority to tailor inventory and services to their market, while the national footprint enables next-day UPS Red Label shipping on many items and access to products from virtually any major electrical manufacturer. The combination of local autonomy, a licensed lighting designer on staff, and a commitment to emergency delivery distinguishes the Williston location in the Vermont market.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical product distribution", "Residential lighting design", "Electrical takeoffs from drawings", "Job management and reporting", "Customer storage and staged delivery", "Emergency same-day delivery", "After-hours and weekend service", "National network sourcing"], "industries": ["Residential electrical contracting", "Commercial electrical contracting"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Next-day shipping via UPS Red Label on many stocked items; emergency same-day delivery available", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["National network of nearly 800 locations enabling next-day shipping on many items", "Local manager authority over inventory and service offerings", "Licensed lighting designer providing residential lighting plans", "Emergency same-day delivery with after-hours and weekend availability", "Customer storage with staged delivery to job sites"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1957 in California -> /", "Nearly 800 locations across America -> /", "Motto: Service. Integrity. Reliability. -> /", "Local managers empowered to make decisions -> /", "Represent top gear lines in the industry -> /", "Products: gear packages, service entrance bills of material, load centers, disconnects, meter mains, circuit breakers -> /", "Location: 399 Shunpike Rd, Williston, VT 05495 -> /", "Phone:  -> /", "Hours: Mon-Fri 6AM-4PM -> /", "Next-day shipping via UPS Red Label -> /", "Licensed lighting designer