UPDATE companies SET description='Cal-Maine Foods, Inc. is headquartered in Ridgeland, Mississippi. The company traces its roots to 1957 when Fred R. Adams Jr. founded an egg operation in Jackson, Mississippi. In 1996, the company went public on NASDAQ under the ticker CALM and has since pursued a disciplined acquisition strategy, integrating 26 companies since 1989 to expand its production footprint.

The company produces conventional and specialty shell eggs — including cage-free, organic, free-range, pasture-raised, and nutritionally enhanced varieties — as well as prepared egg-based foods, ready-to-eat egg products, and breakfast foods under brands such as Eggland’s Best, Land O’Lakes, Farmhouse Eggs, Crepini, and Van’s Foods. Its operations span 2 breeding facilities, 2 hatcheries, 31 feed mills, 51 shell egg production facilities, 38 pullet growing facilities, 52 processing and packaging facilities, and 5 food manufacturing facilities across multiple states. As of May 2026, the company managed approximately 50 million laying hens, recorded $2.9 billion in annual net sales, and sold 1.2 billion dozen eggs.

Cal-Maine serves retail grocery and foodservice channels nationwide, supplying both consumer-facing brands and ingredient eggs to food manufacturers. Its customer base includes major retailers, foodservice distributors, and commercial food processors.

The company states its purpose is to be the consumer-driven provider of nutritious, affordable, and sustainable eggs and egg-based foods that fit today’s lifestyles, with a vision to ensure healthy, affordable egg choices are accessible to every household every day. It also emphasizes commitments to sustainable operations, hunger relief, and strong corporate governance.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Breeding", "Feed milling", "Hatching", "Pullet growing", "Shell egg production", "Processing and packaging", "Food manufacturing", "Specialty egg production (cage-free, organic, free-range, pasture-raised, nutritionally enhanced)", "Prepared egg products manufacturing", "Ready-to-eat egg products", "Breakfast foods manufacturing"], "industries": ["Egg production", "Prepared foods", "Food manufacturing", "Retail grocery", "Foodservice"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "1.2 billion dozen eggs annually (fiscal 2026)", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest egg company in the United States", "Nationwide network of integrated production, processing, and packaging facilities", "Portfolio spanning conventional, specialty, and prepared egg products", "Disciplined acquisition strategy with 26 integrations since 1989", "Commitment to sustainable operations and greenhouse gas emissions reduction"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Ridgeland, Mississippi -> /about-us", "Founded 1957 by Fred R. Adams Jr. in Jackson, Mississippi -> /about-us, /", "Public since 1996 (NASDAQ: CALM) -> /, db", "26 acquisitions since 1989 -> /, db", "Product portfolio: conventional, specialty, prepared eggs -> /about-us, /", "Brands: Eggland\u2019s Best, Land O\u2019Lakes, Farmhouse Eggs, Crepini, Van\u2019s Foods -> /about-us", "Facility counts and types (breeding, feed mills, hatcheries, pullet, shell egg, processing, food manufacturing) -> /about-us", "50 million laying hens, $2.9B net sales, 1.2B dozen eggs sold (fiscal 2026) -> /, /about-u