hting -> /", "Small business -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Caltronics is a leading PCBA company specializing in PCB assembly and electronic design for 30 years.", "founded_year": "1995", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='caltronics-design-assembly' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Capital Electro Circuits Inc., based in Gaithersburg, Maryland, has been fabricating printed circuit boards since 1985. The company operates as a domestic manufacturer of rigid, flexible, and rigid‑flex PCBs, with a focus on specialty designs that fall outside standard fabrication lines.

The shop produces multilayer boards up to 16 layers, with finished thicknesses up to 1.300 inches, and offers advanced features such as blind/buried vias, edge plating, castellations, and controlled‑impedance structures. It works with a wide range of high‑frequency and high‑reliability laminates — including Rogers, Taconic, Arlon, and TMM series — and provides a full suite of surface finishes (HASL, ENIG, ENEPIG, hard gold, immersion tin/silver). In‑house capabilities cover CAM/DFM, drilling, plating, etching, LPI soldermask, legend printing, CNC routing and scoring, and electrical test (continuity/isolation up to 250 VDC).

The company serves aerospace and defense (including programs for Northrop Grumman, BAE Systems, NASA, Lockheed Martin, Honeywell, Sandia National Laboratories, Booz Allen Hamilton, and the U.S. Army), medical imaging and diagnostics, telecommunications (5G and satellite), automotive and electric‑vehicle systems, and RF/microwave applications up to 100 GHz. It emphasizes 100 % U.S.‑based production for military and avionics work.

Capital Electro Circuits differentiates itself by taking on “specialty” jobs that lack defined manufacturing methods, developing custom processes to deliver working parts on short notice. It maintains ISO 9001:2015 certification, UL recognition, RoHS compliance, ITAR registration, and a conflict‑minerals sourcing policy, and offers blanket orders with split deliveries.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ITAR','RoHS','UL Certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Rigid PCB fabrication", "Flexible PCB fabrication", "Rigid\u2011flex PCB fabrication", "Multilayer PCB fabrication (up to 16 layers)", "Blind/buried via fabrication (sequential lamination)", "Thick board fabrication (up to 1.300\u2033 finished thickness)", "High voltage PCB fabrication", "RF/microwave PCB fabrication", "Teflon/PTFE PCB fabrication", "Aluminum/brass/copper heat sink circuit fabrication", "Edge plating", "Castellations", "Controlled impedance manufacturing", "CNC routing and milling", "Panel routing and scoring", "CAM/DFM services", "Drilling (min 0.008\u2033, aspect ratio 12:1)", "Plating (electroless copper, pattern plating up to 6 oz outer/4 oz inner)", "Etching/imaging (min conductor width 0.003\u2033)", "LPI soldermask application", "Legend printing", "Surface finishes: HASL, lead\u2011free HASL, ENIG, ENEPIG, hard gold, immersion tin, immersion silver, electrolytic nickel/gold", "Electrical test (continuity 10 \u03a9, isolation 10 M\u03a9, 10\u2011250 VDC)", "Blanket orders and split deliveries"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Defense", "Medical & Healthcare", "Telecommunications", "Automotive & EVs", "RF & Microwave Applications"], "materials": ["FR-4, FR406, FR408, BT", "Polyimides, GETEK", "Rogers/Arlon 3000/4000/5000/6000 series", "Arlon CuClad, DiClad, AD series", "Non-woven and woven PTFE", "RO4000, RO4350", "TMM3, TMM4, TMM6, TMM10, TMM10I", "Taconic TLY, TLX, TLE, TLC, TLT, RF-35", "Ceramic-filled PTFE", "IsoClad 900 series", "Polyclad FR-250HR, PCL-FR-370HR, PCL-LD-