UPDATE companies SET description='Capitol Iron Works operates from Gaithersburg, Maryland, in the heart of the Washington, D.C. metropolitan area. The company was founded in August 2014 by Ronald Vargas, who serves as president and co-owner. Vargas immigrated to the United States from Nicaragua in 2004 and learned welding on the job at Bethesda Iron Works, eventually earning his welding certification before launching his own venture, initially named Capitol Iron Solutions.

The shop specializes in custom ornamental and architectural metalwork, producing railings, stairs, handrails, glass and cable railings, steel fencing, balconies, canopies, and automatic gates. It works with stainless steel, aluminum, bronze, structural steel, wrought iron, and glass, offering powder-coat finishes. The 4,300-square-foot facility houses three fabrication units and a staff of 14. Project values range from $1,000 to $500,000, with revenue projected at $1.5 million for 2018.

Capitol Iron Works serves residential, commercial, and government clients across the D.C., Maryland, and Virginia region. Notable government work includes fabrication and installation of bronze railings for the Rayburn House Office Building under contract with the Architect of the Capitol, the federal agency responsible for the U.S. Capitol Complex. The company also handles restoration of historic metalwork.

Vargas attributes the firm’s rapid growth to customer service, on-time delivery, and a stable, skilled workforce—only one employee has left in four years. He emphasizes a willingness to tackle complex, challenging projects that other shops might avoid, combining fabrication, installation, and restoration under one roof.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom ornamental metalwork", "Architectural railing fabrication", "Stair and handrail fabrication", "Glass railing fabrication", "Cable railing fabrication", "Steel fencing fabrication", "Balcony fabrication", "Canopy fabrication", "Automatic gate fabrication", "Structural steel fabrication", "Glass fabrication", "Custom welding", "Metal cutting and shaping", "Decorative metal detailing", "Powder coating", "Installation services", "Restoration of historic metalwork", "Design consultation", "Site assessment and measurement"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Government facilities", "Architectural metalwork"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Bronze", "Structural steel", "Glass", "Wrought iron", "Powder coating"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Emphasis on customer service and communication", "Commitment to on-schedule delivery and meeting deadlines", "High employee retention (only one departure in four years)", "Full in-house capability from design through installation and restoration", "Willingness to accept complex, technically demanding projects"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Gaithersburg, Maryland -> db", "Founded August 2014 -> /about-us", "Founder Ronald Vargas, president and co-owner -> /about-us", "14 employees -> /about-us", "4,300-square-foot facility with three fabrication units -> /about-us", "Custom ornamental metalwork: railings, stairs, handrails, glass/cable railings, fencing, balconies, canopies, automatic gates -> /about-us and /", "Materials: stainless steel, aluminum, bronze, structural steel, glass, wrought iron, powder coating -> /about-us and /", "Government client: Architect of the Capitol, Rayburn House Office Building bronze railings -> /about-us", "Serves DMV area (DC, Maryland, Virginia) -> /", "Project range $1,000 to $500,000 -> /about-us", "Revenue projected $1.5M for 2018 -> /about-us", "Employee retention: only one left in four years -> /about-us", "Customer service and on-time delivery emphasis -> /about-us", "Full-service: design, fabrication, installation, restoration -> /about-us and /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Capitol Iron Works specializes in custom ornamental metalwork projects based on unique design ideas, working with ferrous and nonferrous metals, such as stainless steel, aluminum and bronze.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "14", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='capitol-iron-works' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company focuses on healthcare informatics, providing a vendor-neutral platform that connects medical devices and clinical systems across hospital enterprises.

The company’s portfolio spans medical device integration, clinical surveillance, patient monitoring, virtual care, retrospective analytics, and clinical information systems. Its platform captures live-streaming data from over 1,200 medical devices — including measurements, settings, alarms, and waveforms — and delivers it using industry-standard protocols to more than 100 downstream systems such as electronic health records, clinical information systems, and alarm management tools. Key product lines include Philips Axon, Capsule Neuron, Capsule Vitals Stream, Chart Xpress, the Medical Device Information Platform, eCareManager, Clinical Insights Manager, Capsule Surveillance, and IntelliSpace Critical Care and Anesthesia (ICCA).

Capsule serves hospitals and health systems worldwide, with installations at organizations such as Hamilton Health Sciences in Canada, CoxHealth in the United States, and Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust in the United Kingdom. Its solutions target acute care environments including intensive care units, perioperative settings, and general wards, aiming to reduce clinician burnout and improve patient outcomes through automated data capture and clinical decision support.

The company emphasizes its vendor-neutral, open ecosystem approach, which allows healthcare providers to leverage existing infrastructure while expanding capabilities incrementally. It also highlights deep clinical and operational experience, stating that its support extends beyond technology to fit workflows and enable clinical staff rather than burden them.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical device integration", "Clinical surveillance", "Patient monitoring", "Virtual care (eCareManager)", "Retrospective analytics (Clinical Insights Manager)", "Clinical information system (IntelliSpace Critical Care and Anesthesia)", "System integration engine", "Cloud data storage and analytics", "Intensive care patient data management", "Perioperative patient data management", "Connectivity management (Philips Axon, Capsule Neuron, Capsule Vitals Stream, Chart Xpress)", "Medical device information platform", "Alarm management", "Clinical decision support", "Documentation and workflow automation"], "industries": ["Medical Device Integration", "Medical Device Information Platform"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Philips Axon", "Capsule Neuron", "Capsule Vitals Stream", "Chart Xpress", "Medical Device Information Platform", "eCareManager", "Clinical Insights Manager", "Capsule Surveillance", "IntelliSpace Critical Care and Anesthesia"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vendor-neutral, open ecosystem connecting over 1,200 medical devices to 100+ clinical systems", "Broad portfolio spanning medical device integration, clinical surveillance, virtual care, and analytics", "Deep clinical and operational experience with support tailored to existing workflows", "Proven installations at major health systems including Hamilton Health Sciences, CoxHealth, and Cambridge University Hospitals"], "facts_used": ["Company name and parent: Philips Capsule part of Philips Acute Care Informatics -> db", "Headquarters: Cambridge, Massachusetts -> db", "Platform connects over 1,200 medical devices to 100+ systems -> /", "Product lines: Philips Axon, Capsule Neuron, Capsule Vitals Stream, Chart Xpress, Medical Device Information Platform, eCareManager, Clinical Insights Manager, Capsule Surveillance, IntelliSpace Critical Care and Anesthesia -> /", "Customer examples: Hamilton Health Sciences, CoxHealth, Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust -> /", "Industries served: Medical Device Integration, Medical Device Information Platform -> db", "Capabilities: Medical Device Integration, Clinical Surveillance, Patient Monitoring, Virtual Care, Retrospective Analytics, Clinical Information System -> /", "Vendor-neutral, open ecosystem differentiator -> /", "Deep clinical and operational experience -> /"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Our portfolio of informatics solutions\u2014medical device integration, system integration engine, cloud data storage and analytics, clinical surveillance, intensive care and perioperative patient data management, and virtual care\u2014provides not just individual products, but a suite of applications that seamlessly integrate with each other and your existing hospital systems.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='capsule-technologies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Captor Corporation was established in 1965 in Tipp City, Ohio, by an engineering-oriented management team that included several experienced veterans. The founders brought deep expertise in electronic filters and military-aerospace communications, and early success allowed the company to build a dedicated manufacturing facility that has since expanded to 35,000 square feet.

The company designs and manufactures custom EMI and EMC filtering solutions, including TEMPEST, HEMP/EMP, and signal-line filters, as well as custom capacitors, inductors, coils, cable assemblies, wire harnesses, electromechanical box builds, and power distribution units. All engineering, production, and testing occur in-house at the Tipp City facility, which houses an advanced all-welded shielded room for pre-compliance testing. Captor has produced over 10,000 custom filter designs and focuses on low-to-medium-volume production.

Captor serves OEMs in aerospace, defense, secure communications, medical equipment, telecommunications, radar systems, and missile-launching programs.

The company emphasizes that custom solutions can be delivered faster and more cost-effectively than many competitors'' catalog parts, with no added cost for tailoring. Its mission centers on producing the highest-quality EMI filters, exceeding customer expectations, and maintaining a safe, respectful workplace while continuously improving quality and profitability.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','MIL-STD-220','MIL-STD-461 CE102']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom EMI filter design and manufacturing", "Custom TEMPEST filter manufacturing", "Custom HEMP/EMP filter manufacturing", "Custom telephone and signal line filter manufacturing", "Custom capacitor winding and manufacturing", "Custom inductor and coil manufacturing (toroid, bobbin-wound, tube-wound, C-core)", "Military cable assembly manufacturing (ISO-compliant, MIL-SPEC)", "Wire harness manufacturing", "Electromechanical assembly (box builds, integrated systems, electrical control panels)", "Power distribution unit manufacturing (cabinet, floor-mounted, rack-mounted, portable)", "In-house qualification and acceptance testing (altitude, humidity, thermal shock, vibration, hermetic seal, electrical ATP)", "Reverse engineering of electronic assemblies", "PCB layout and design (3D CAD, 2D CAD, PCAD)", "Shielded facility room EMI filtering", "MIL-COTS filter manufacturing", "Military electronic mechanical assembly", "Infrastructure hardening (IT security)", "SCIF (Sensitive Compartmented Information Facility) solutions"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense / Military", "Secure communications", "Medical equipment", "Telecommunications", "Radar systems", "Missile launching systems", "Industrial applications"], "materials": ["Capacitor films and foils", "Aluminum", "Wire (4/0 to 32 AWG)", "Corrosion-resistant materials"], "equipment": ["Standard and custom-built capacitor winding equipment", "Advanced all-welded shielded room", "3D CAD, 2D CAD, PCAD software"], "volume": "Low to medium volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 10,000 custom filter designs in portfolio", "Custom solutions often faster and more cost-effective than competitors'' catalog parts", "In-house engineering, production, and testing under one roof", "35,000 sq ft facility with advanced all-welded shielded room for pre-compliance testing", "Proprietary capacitor winding equipment enabling virtually unlimited design configurations"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1965 -> /about-us", "35,000 sq ft facility -> /about-us", "Over 10,000 custom filter designs -> /capabilities", "Industries: aerospace, defense, secure communications, medical, telecommunications -> / and /capabilities", "Certifications: ISO9001, AS9100 -> db and /capabilities", "Capabilities list -> /capabilities", "Custom capacitor winding equipment -> /about-us", "Shielded room -> /about-us", "Testing capabilities -> /capabilities", "Volume: low to medium -> /about-us", "MIL-STD-220, MIL-STD-461 CE102 -> /capabilities", "Wire sizes 4/0 to 32 AWG -> /capabilities", "PDU types -> /capabilities", "SCIF -> / and /capabilities", "Infrastructure hardening -> /capabilities"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Captor Corporation engineers and manufactures EMI filter solutions and custom electromechanical assemblies for OEMs operating in aerospace, defense, and secure communications environments", "founded_year": "1965", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='captor-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
