], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "specializes in food service equipment and supplies, sales and service", "founded_year": "1997", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='carney-sloan-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Carnico Foods LLC operates a USDA-inspected meat processing facility in Litchfield, Michigan. The company was created at the beginning of 2022 by the owners of Ferry Farms, a local farming operation, who expanded into wholesale distribution through Ferry Farms Wholesale. Facing a persistent shortage of USDA-inspected processing and co-packing capacity, they established Carnico to serve farms and food businesses across southern Michigan.

The facility provides processing, secondary packaging, private labeling, co-packing, and product development services. It is equipped for smoking meats and features a state-of-the-art drying and climatic room for producing specialty sausages and cured meats. The plant also offers flavor and recipe development for clients.

Carnico’s customer base includes local farms, retail outlets, and wholesale distributors. The facility serves similar businesses throughout the region.

The company was founded specifically to remove the bottleneck of limited USDA-inspected processing for small and mid-sized meat producers. Its founders, who were farmers first, built the operation to provide accessible, full-service processing and co-packing for the local agricultural community.', certifications=ARRAY['USDA inspected']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Meat processing", "Secondary packaging", "Private labeling", "Co-packing", "Product development", "Flavor and recipe development", "Smoking", "Drying and climatic curing"], "industries": ["Meat processing", "Agriculture (local farms)", "Food wholesale", "Food retail"], "materials": ["Beef", "Pork", "Meat", "Spices", "Beer"], "equipment": ["Drying/climatic room", "Smoking equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["USDA-inspected processing facility", "State-of-the-art drying and climatic room for cured meats", "In-house smoking capability", "Private labeling and co-packing services", "Flavor and recipe development support"], "facts_used": ["Founded beginning of 2022 -> /about-us", "Headquarters Litchfield, Michigan -> db", "Locally owned and operated -> /", "Majority owners were farmers (Ferry Farms) -> /about-us", "USDA-inspected meat processing facility -> /", "Services: processing, packaging, private labeling, co-packing, product development -> /", "Smoking and drying/climatic room for specialty sausages and cured meats -> /", "Serves local farms and retail/wholesale businesses in southern Michigan -> /", "Ferry Farms Wholesale products: snack sticks, jerky, charcuterie, bacon, ground beef patties, hot dogs, beer brats -> /about-us", "Flavor & recipe development offered -> /", "Secondary packaging offered -> /", "Private labeling offered -> /", "Co-packaging offered -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Carnico Foods is a locally owned and operated, USDA-inspected meat processing facility that was created at the beginning of 2022. Carnico will serve as a processing, packaging, private labeling, co-packing, and product development facility...", "founded_year": "2022", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='carnico-foods-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Carolina Chain & Cable, LLC operates from Aberdeen, North Carolina. ALP Industries itself was founded in 1981 by Reitzel Swaim and Ron Space in Parkesburg, Pennsylvania, and later relocated to Coatesville, Pennsylvania. In 2022, ALP Industries became part of Lift Solutions Holdings, a national provider of industrial lifting solutions.

As part of the ALP Industries network, the Aberdeen location participates in the distribution and sale of industrial lifting products, including slings, chain, and cable. The company also provides OSHA-mandated inspections, aftermarket services, and parts for overhead cranes and other lifting equipment, as well as offering crane equipment. The parent company maintains a multi‑site footprint with facilities in Aberdeen, NC; Parkesburg, PA; Duncan, SC; and several other U.S. locations.

The company serves customers in need of industrial lifting solutions, particularly those requiring sling and rigging products, overhead crane inspections, and replacement parts.

