UPDATE companies SET description='Carolina Solar Energy was founded in 2004 in Durham, North Carolina, by Richard Harkrader, an architect emeritus, building contractor, and real estate developer. The family-owned business began with a goal to demonstrate that renewable energy portfolio standards could build a solar industry in the state. Richard’s early trial-and-error project development led to the first utility-scale solar project in the Southeast, completed at NC State in 2007.

The company develops utility-scale photovoltaic (PV) solar projects across the Southeast and Gulf South, managing site selection, interconnection applications, state permitting, and community outreach. As of the latest figures, over 950 MWdc of projects are operating or under construction. The team handles landowner relations, project management, and policy advocacy, working with municipal partners, utilities, and landowners to bring projects from concept to operation.

Carolina Solar Energy serves utilities, municipal governments, county economic development agencies, and multi-generational landowners in the Southern and Gulf South regions. Notable partners include the City of Raleigh, which completed its first major solar development with the company, and Person County, which hosts three photovoltaic facilities totaling approximately five megawatts. The firm also collaborates with clean energy membership organizations on state and national policy.

The company was started to prove that legislative frameworks could create a viable solar market in North Carolina, and it continues to emphasize early-market entry and community acceptance. Leadership highlights a balance of renewable energy expertise, engineering, installation capability, and financial knowledge as differentiators, along with a rehabilitative workforce partnership with TROSA.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Utility-scale photovoltaic (PV) project development", "Site selection and due diligence", "Interconnection application and state permitting", "Landowner outreach and community relations", "Policy advocacy for utility-scale solar", "Project management and construction oversight"], "industries": ["Solar energy", "Renewable energy", "Utilities", "Government", "Land development"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First utility-scale solar project in the Southeast (2007)", "Over 950 MWdc of projects operating or under construction", "First to apply for Kentucky state-level solar permits (2020)", "Family-owned with focus on multi-generational landowners", "Active policy advocacy for utility-scale solar at state and national levels"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2004 by Richard Harkrader -> /about", "Headquarters in Durham, NC -> db", "Family-owned business -> /about", "First utility-scale solar project in Southeast (2007) -> /about", "Over 950 MWdc operating or under construction -> /", "First to apply for Kentucky state-level solar permits (2020) -> /about", "Develops utility-scale PV projects across Southeast and Gulf South -> /about", "Site selection, interconnection applications, state permitting -> /about", "Landowner outreach and community relations -> /about", "Policy advocacy for utility-scale solar -> /", "Partners: City of Raleigh, Person County -> /", "Workforce partnership with TROSA -> /", "CEO Carson Harkrader leads since 2018 -> /about", "Team includes Tyler Caron, Vann Joines, Benjamin Finch -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We develop utility-scale photovoltaic (PV) solar energy projects across the Southeastern US.", "founded_year": "2004", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='carolina-solar-energy-iii-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Carolina Woodworks operates from Lyman, South Carolina, in the Upstate region. The family-owned shop draws on more than 30 years of hands-on experience and multi-generational woodworking knowledge, with a background in custom home building that informs its approach to cabinetry and millwork.

The company designs, builds, finishes, and installs fully custom cabinetry, built-ins, vanities, entertainment walls, commercial millwork, and architectural details. Every project is fabricated in-house using premium materials, BLUM soft-close hardware, dovetailed drawer boxes, and professional lacquer finishes. The shop works across frameless, face-frame, inset, and multiple overlay cabinet configurations.

Carolina Woodworks serves homeowners, builders, remodelers, interior designers, and commercial clients throughout the Upstate. Its portfolio includes custom kitchens, bathrooms, built-in shelving, entertainment centers, office suites, and pantry systems for both residential and commercial spaces.

The firm emphasizes exact-design flexibility—building each piece around the home''s architecture rather than a catalog—along with technical range that covers multiple cabinet styles under one roof. Furniture-grade execution, precision joinery, specialized finishes, and direct client communication with visible progress are cited as core differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinetry design and fabrication", "Architectural millwork", "Kitchen cabinet fabrication", "Bathroom cabinet fabrication", "Built-in cabinetry", "Entertainment center fabrication", "Office suite cabinetry", "Pantry cabinetry", "Commercial millwork", "In-house finishing (lacquer)", "Dovetail joinery", "BLUM soft-close hardware installation", "Installation services", "Cabinet style configuration (frameless, face-frame, inset, overlay)"], "industries": ["Homeowners", "Builders", "Remodelers", "Interior designers", "Commercial clients"], "materials": ["Premium materials", "Solid wood", "BLUM soft-close hardware", "Dovetailed drawer boxes", "Professional lacquer finishes"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Exact-design flexibility: every cabinet constructed around the home, architecture, and client\u2014not a catalog", "Technical range: frameless, face-frame, inset, and multiple overlay configurations under one shop", "Furniture-grade execution: premium materials, precision joinery, specialized finishes, architectural detailing", "Personal accountability: direct communication, collaborative design, visible progress, disciplined installation", "30+ years of hands-on experience and multi-generational woodworking knowledge"], "facts_used": ["Location: Lyman, South Carolina -> db", "Family-owned -> /", "30+ years of hands-on experience and multi-generational woodworking knowledge -> /", "Designs, builds, finishes, and installs fully custom cabinetry, built-ins, vanities, entertainment walls, commercial millwork,