UPDATE companies SET description='Carolina Yarn and Fabrics, LLC, based in Laurens, South Carolina, has been a manufacturer and principal supplier of highly engineered fabric-formed concrete erosion control and scour protection systems since the ARMORFORM® trade name was established in 1984. The company draws together teams of project managers, engineers, and production and field service managers dedicated to sustainable solutions.

The firm produces ARMORFORM® fabric-formed concrete systems, which use double-layer woven geo-textiles engineered exclusively as forms for casting concrete erosion control revetments and linings. The geo-textiles are woven from polyester and/or nylon yarns and designed with specific mechanical and hydraulic properties. Installation involves positioning the fabric forms and pumping high-strength, fine-aggregate concrete, either underwater or on dry land.

The company serves engineering firms, government agencies, and commercial clients across infrastructure, water, environment, industry, and energy sectors. Notable references include acceptance by the Mine Safety and Health Administration for mining facilities in 1993, U.S. Navy approval for underwater ballast and protection of pipelines and communication cables in 2002, and exclusive collaboration with the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers on scour protection for the Olmsted Locks and Dam in 2008.

Carolina Yarn and Fabrics emphasizes engineered products, comprehensive technical support, and responsive delivery, which the company says have resulted in most projects being repeat work with long-standing clients. The focus on sustainable solutions for infrastructure, water, environment, industry, and energy underpins its approach.', certifications=ARRAY['MSHA accepted for mining facilities']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fabric-formed concrete erosion control", "Scour protection systems", "Lining applications", "Double-layer woven geo-textile manufacturing", "Concrete pumping and installation", "Project management", "Engineering support", "Field service management"], "industries": ["Infrastructure", "Water", "Environment", "Industry", "Energy", "Mining", "Defense", "Civil construction", "Government", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Polyester yarn", "Nylon yarn", "High-strength fine aggregate concrete"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fabric-formed concrete systems that can be installed underwater or on dry land", "Double-layer woven geo-textiles engineered exclusively as concrete forms", "Comprehensive technical support and responsive delivery driving repeat client work", "MSHA acceptance for mining facilities and U.S. Navy approval for underwater ballast", "Over 50 million square feet installed globally since 1984"], "facts_used": ["Company name, location, and manufacturer description -> db", "ARMORFORM trade name established 1984 -> /", "Double-layer woven geo-textiles from polyester/nylon yarns -> /", "Installation by positioning forms and pumping concrete underwater or on land -> /", "Cumulative installed square footage milestones (10M, 30M, 50M SF) -> /", "Endicott Island, AK project 1989 (Arctic Circle) -> /", "MSHA acceptance 1993 for mining facilities -> /", "US Navy approval 2002 for underwater ballast and pipeline/cable protection -> /", "USACE exclusive collaboration 2008 for Olmsted Locks & Dam -> /", "NOVA Award 2012 for Olmsted Dam Project -> /", "Industries served: infrastructure, water, environment, industry, energy -> /", "Client types: engineering, government, commercial -> /", "Repeat work with long-standing clients due to technical support and delivery -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Carolina Yarn and Fabrics, LLC, based in Laurens, SC, is a leading manufacturer and principal supplier of highly engineered fabric-formed concrete erosion control and scour protection systems.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='carolina-yarn-fabrics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Carpenter Co. is headquartered in Moore, Oklahoma, and traces its origins to 1950 when it began as a local latex foam manufacturer. The company has since grown into the world''s largest vertically integrated producer of polyurethane foams, operating a network of more than 60 production locations worldwide.

The company manufactures polyurethane chemical solutions, polyester fibers, and insulation materials, with a core focus on flexible urethane foams. Its vertical integration includes production of polyether polyols, a key foam component. Carpenter employs approximately 6,500 people globally and backs its operations with state-of-the-art research and development facilities in Richmond, where expert teams design innovative products and conduct rigorous in-house testing.

Carpenter serves a diversified global marketplace, with a highlighted focus on the medical field through tailored protection solutions. Its products also support bedding and furniture applications, as evidenced by the patent-pending Casper Core+ technology aimed at improving mattress recyclability. The company''s domestic mattress manufacturing operations are noted to support American jobs and local communities.

