UPDATE companies SET description='Century Mold was founded in 1986 in Shelbyville, Tennessee. The company operates as a U.S.-based manufacturer of precision plastic components, serving customers across North America from six production facilities.

The company provides fully integrated services from part and tool design through production and finishing. Its capabilities include injection molding on presses up to 2,200 tons, vertical and horizontal molding, multi-material (two-shot and overmold), insert molding, gas-assist, and MuCell processes. Secondary operations cover assembly, balancing, vibration welding, sonic welding, hot plate welding, heat stake welding, pad printing, and performance testing. Engineering support encompasses design for manufacturability, Moldflow and finite element analysis, reverse engineering, scanning, and 3D printing. The facilities total 675,000 square feet and house more than 200 presses, supported by a team of over 50 engineers, designers, and mold builders.

Century Mold serves automotive, defense, industrial, consumer, and lawn-and-garden markets. In automotive, it supplies complex, high-volume components found in over 80 percent of vehicles on U.S. roads, working with OEMs and Tier 1 suppliers such as BorgWarner, Robert Bosch, Delphi, and Visteon. For defense, it provides mission-critical parts with secure, fully controlled U.S. production. Industrial and consumer customers rely on its in-house design and engineering expertise to bring products to market.

The company emphasizes a localized supply chain and in-house expertise to deliver consistent quality, on-time performance, and cost efficiency. It holds ISO 9001:2015 and IATF 16949 certifications and has earned multiple Supplier of the Year awards from major automotive OEMs.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','IATF 16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design for manufacturability", "Moldflow analysis", "Finite element analysis", "Reverse engineering", "3D scanning", "3D printing", "Injection molding (up to 2,200 tons)", "Vertical molding", "Horizontal molding", "Multi-material molding (2-shot)", "Overmolding", "Insert molding", "Gas-assist molding", "MuCell molding", "Assembly", "Balancing", "Vibration welding", "Sonic welding", "Hot plate welding", "Heat stake welding", "Pad printing", "Performance and validation testing", "Tool design", "Tool transfer management"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Defense", "Industrial", "Consumer", "Lawn and Garden"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Six production facilities across North America", "50+ engineers, designers, and mold builders on staff", "675,000 sq ft of production capacity with 200+ presses up to 2,200 tons", "IATF 16949 and ISO 9001:2015 certified", "Recognized by major automotive OEMs with Supplier of the Year awards"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1986 -> db", "Headquarters Shelbyville, Tennessee -> db", "6 production facilities across North America -> /", "675,000 sq ft production capacity -> /about-us", "200+ injection molding presses up to 2,200 tons -> /about-us", "50+ engineers, designers, and mold builders -> /about-us", "ISO 9001:2015 and IATF 16949 certified -> /", "Serves automotive, defense, industrial, consumer, lawn and garden -> /", "Automotive customers include BorgWarner, Robert Bosch, Delphi, Visteon -> /", "Capabilities: injection molding, multi-material, insert, gas-assist, MuCell, secondary operations -> /capabilities", "D