UPDATE companies SET description='Certified Parts Corporation (CPC) was founded in 1982 by James Grafft in Edgerton, Wisconsin. The company traces its roots to 1974 when Grafft worked at Fox Corporation in Janesville and recognized the need for continuous parts supply for manufacturers that had ceased operations. In 1976 he purchased Fox''s service-parts division and the Bridgestone brand on his 26th birthday.

Today CPC operates a 200,000-square-foot factory in Edgerton where it manufactures original service parts — carburetors, the full line of Comet torque converters and clutches, and other components — for a portfolio that includes Comet, TecumsehPower, Wisconsin Wagon, and vintage recreational-vehicle brands. The company also owns historic motorcycle and mini-cycle marques such as Bridgestone, Indian, Rupp, Chaparral and Steen, and supplies hard-to-find engine parts for snowmobiles and mini-cycles. Production volumes support both OEM contracts and aftermarket distribution through a worldwide dealer network.

CPC serves OEM manufacturers in the recreational, construction, agricultural and marine sectors, as well as dealers and end users maintaining vintage equipment. Its customer base includes original equipment builders that integrate Comet clutches into new products and a global service network that supports TecumsehPower, Lauson and Snow King engines.

The business was built on a passion for history and an eye for opportunity: Grafft''s strategy of acquiring orphaned brands, restarting production and re-establishing dealer channels has returned multiple legacy names to active manufacturing.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Legacy brand acquisition and revival", "Service parts manufacturing", "OEM component supply", "Carburetor production", "Torque converter and clutch manufacturing (Comet line)", "Engine parts production (TecumsehPower, Lauson, Snow King)", "Vintage recreational vehicle parts supply", "Global distribution and dealer network management"], "industries": ["Recreational vehicles", "Construction equipment", "Agricultural equipment", "Marine", "Motorcycle and mini-cycle", "Snowmobile", "Watercraft", "Outdoor power equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Acquires and revives orphaned legacy brands with original tooling and IP", "Manufactures genuine service parts in a 200,000 sq ft facility", "Supplies OEMs across recreational, construction, agricultural and marine markets", "Maintains a worldwide dealer and distributor network for vintage and current products", "Owns historic motorcycle, snowmobile, watercraft and engine brands"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 by James Grafft in Edgerton, Wisconsin -> db", "200,000 sq ft factory in Edgerton, WI -> /", "Owns brands: Comet, TecumsehPower, Wisconsin Wagon, vintage recreational vehicle parts, motorcycle/mini-cycle brands -> /", "Manufactures carburetors, Comet torque converters and clutches -> /", "Supplies OEMs in recreational, construction, agricultural, marine industries -> /", "Worldwide dealer network -> /", "Jay Grafft promoted to President in 2021 -> /", "Featured in Rock County Roots 2018 -> /", "30th birthday 2012 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Initially specializing in manufacturing service parts for these companies, CPC has grown into a major supplier to OEM''s and has brought some of these brands back into production.", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='certified-parts-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Chairmans Foods LLC is based in Nashville, Tennessee. The company specializes in producing high-quality entrées, main dishes, sides, soups, queso, and more for foodservice operators and retail stores.

The company offers custom production of bulk recipes and exact duplication of proprietary products at national scale. With hundreds of proven recipes and a proprietary product development process, Chairmans Foods manufactures bulk prepared foods including side dishes, sauces, queso, soups, chili, and deli entrée ingredients. Its capabilities cover specialty proteins, soups, sides, breakfast items, and desserts, delivering consistent, high-quality products that reduce labor and operating costs for customers.

Chairmans Foods serves foodservice operators, retail stores, and restaurant customers. Its products are designed for operators and retailers seeking quality bulk comfort foods, and the company works with clients to develop custom solutions tailored to their needs.

