UPDATE companies SET description='Champlain Metals was founded in 2004 by John Marius in Burlington, Vermont. Marius, who trained with the French artisans’ guild Compagnons du Devoir, brought a tradition of ornamental metalwork learned in the Champagne and Alsatian regions of France to the Champlain Valley.

The company provides design, fabrication, casting, and forging services for structural and ornamental metalwork. Its capabilities include architectural metal work, custom metal fabrication, bronze and iron casting, and forging of components such as brackets, railings, and stair stringers. The shop states it can handle production runs, though specific facility size, headcount, or annual volume are not disclosed.

Champlain Metals works with architects, builders, and private clients on projects ranging from custom side tables and garden trowels to heat exchangers and forged bronze cap rails. Past projects include stair stringers for a contractor named Andrew Russel, a heat exchanger for a residential client, and ornamental brackets for awning installations. The firm’s portfolio also features forged bronze details and iron pour samples.

Marius emphasizes an “old world passion for detail” rooted in European guild training as the firm’s distinguishing characteristic. The business was started to continue that tradition of hand‑crafted metalwork in Vermont, offering both one‑off artistic pieces and repeatable production work.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Architectural metal work", "Custom metal fabrication", "Casting", "Forging", "Design services", "Structural metal work", "Ornamental metal work"], "industries": ["Architectural metalwork", "Structural metalwork", "Ornamental metalwork", "Custom fabrication"], "materials": ["Bronze", "Iron"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Artisan training with Compagnons du Devoir guild", "French regional metalworking traditions (Champagne, Alsatian)", "Custom structural and ornamental metal fabrication", "Casting and forging in bronze and iron", "Production capacity for repeat orders"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2004 in Burlington, Vermont -> /", "Founder John Marius trained with Compagnons du Devoir guild -> /about", "Offers architectural metal work, custom fabrication, casting, forging -> /", "Serves clients in Champlain Valley and beyond -> /", "Produces custom items such as stair stringers, heat exchangers, forged bronze brackets, side tables, garden trowels -> /", "Emphasizes old world passion for detail from French traditions -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Champlain Metals offers design and metal fabrication solutions for structural and ornamental metal work.", "founded_year": "2004", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='champlain-metals' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Charleston Steel operates from Dunbar, West Virginia, where it has supplied steel to the construction industry since 1989. The company is led by President John E. Goetz IV and describes itself as a full‑service steel company with a customer‑oriented philosophy.

The shop fabricates structural steel for commercial and industrial projects, producing items such as fabricated structural steel, joists and deck, stairs and handrail, simple bridges and bridge components. It also manufactures material‑handling and heavy‑duty weighing equipment, and runs a value‑added steel service center. The facility holds AISC certification and AWS Certified Welding Fabricator status, with welding procedures covering all joints, processes and positions.

