UPDATE companies SET description='Chicana Foods operates from Boise, Idaho, where first-generation Mexican-American photographer Allison Corona founded the company alongside her sisters Claudia and Giovanna and their mother Gloria. The venture draws on traditional family recipes from Mexico, where the founders'' maternal aunts and uncles have run a salsa business for over two decades. Corona adapted her aunt''s salsa macha recipe in her Boise kitchen, launching a line of nut- and chile-based salsas that blend Veracruz and Oaxaca traditions with African influences.

The company produces salsa macha in varieties including peanut and cranberry, using ingredients such as seeds, nuts, chiles, olive oil, and dried fruit.

Chicana Foods sells through specialty grocers, coffee shops, farmers markets, delis, wineries, and museum stores across Idaho and Utah. Retail partners include Coffee and Supply Co. in Eagle, Flying M Coffee locations in Boise, Caldwell, and Nampa, the Boise Farmers Market, Idaho Made, the Idaho State Museum Store, Indian Creek Winery in Kuna, and Das Cafe in Spring City, Utah. The brand also appears on menus at cafes such as Just Be Acai and Common Ground Coffee.

